    "diagnosis": "Breast implant&ndash;associated anaplastic large cell lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Tumour cells are found in a background of fibrinous material adjacent to the inner surface of a fibrous capsule. Although an inflammatory infiltrate with a large component of histiocytes is present in the capsular tissue, infiltration of tumour cells is absent (&lt;&lt;30018&gt;&gt;). Tumour cells in seroma fluid with strands of fibrin material (&lt;&lt;30016&gt;&gt;). Invasion into breast parenchyma. Remnants of breast ducts are extensively infiltrated by large lymphoma cells. This feature is associated with aggressive disease (&lt;&lt;30836&gt;&gt;).",
    "source": "Daphne de Jong",
    "copyright": "",
